    <title>v1.15.3 - API Cleanup</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;This version is backwards compatible to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ava-labs/avalanchego/releases/tag/v1.15.0&quot;&gt;v1.15.0&lt;/a&gt;. It is optional, but encouraged.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The plugin version is unchanged at &lt;code&gt;47&lt;/code&gt; and is compatible with version &lt;code&gt;v1.15.2&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;APIs&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Added a &lt;code&gt;Gas-Used&lt;/code&gt; header to C-Chain &lt;code&gt;/rpc&lt;/code&gt; responses with the total gas used by every completed &lt;code&gt;eth_call&lt;/code&gt; in the request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;admin.lockProfile&lt;/code&gt; and continuous profiling now write &lt;code&gt;lock.profile&lt;/code&gt; in the binary pprof format, like the CPU and memory profiles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Configs&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Added &lt;code&gt;--profile-continuous-mutex-fraction&lt;/code&gt; (default &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;, which keeps the existing behavior) to set the mutex profile fraction used by continuous profiling. Set it to &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; to stop recording mutex contention, or to &lt;code&gt;n&lt;/code&gt; to sample 1 of every n events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Added the &lt;code&gt;filter&lt;/code&gt; API to the C-Chain &lt;code&gt;apis&lt;/code&gt; option. It serves the polling filter methods (&lt;code&gt;eth_newFilter&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;eth_newBlockFilter&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;eth_newPendingTransactionFilter&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;eth_getFilterChanges&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;eth_getFilterLogs&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;eth_uninstallFilter&lt;/code&gt;), which moved out of &lt;code&gt;subscription&lt;/code&gt;. It is enabled by default. A config that sets &lt;code&gt;apis&lt;/code&gt; must add &lt;code&gt;filter&lt;/code&gt; to keep serving these methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Added the &lt;code&gt;logs&lt;/code&gt; API to the C-Chain &lt;code&gt;apis&lt;/code&gt; option. It serves &lt;code&gt;eth_getLogs&lt;/code&gt;, which moved out of &lt;code&gt;subscription&lt;/code&gt;. It is enabled by default. A config that sets &lt;code&gt;apis&lt;/code&gt; must add &lt;code&gt;logs&lt;/code&gt; to keep serving &lt;code&gt;eth_getLogs&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Metrics&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SAE state sync scores peers separately for each sync protocol, so &lt;code&gt;avalanche_evm_p2p_peer_tracker_{num_tracked_peers,num_responsive_peers,average_bandwidth}&lt;/code&gt; are replaced by one set per protocol: &lt;code&gt;avalanche_evm_p2p_peer_tracker_&amp;lt;protocol&amp;gt;_*&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;protocol&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; one of &lt;code&gt;leaf&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;code&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;block&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;cchain_leaf&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Fixes&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed C-Chain log queries (&lt;code&gt;eth_getLogs&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;eth_getFilterLogs&lt;/code&gt;) failing with &lt;code&gt;failed to get logs for block #N&lt;/code&gt; when the range reached an accepted block that had not yet executed. Range queries now stop at the last executed block, and &lt;code&gt;blockHash&lt;/code&gt; queries for an unexecuted block return &lt;code&gt;unknown block&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed &lt;code&gt;admin.stopCPUProfiler&lt;/code&gt; leaving mutex profiling enabled, which kept recording mutex contention until the node restarted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed the C-Chain block builder ordering pending transactions inconsistently. Transactions could be out of effective gas tip order, and a sender&#39;s later nonce could come before an earlier one, which left it out of the block.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed &lt;code&gt;UnmarshalText&lt;/code&gt; implementations which prevented usage of jsonv2 (default in Go 1.27).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
